        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "3 years ago",
        "text": "I was recommended this guy by my plumber who said you need someone like daniel to fix your jacuzzi. Great I love my plumber he's great.\nDaniel comes over.. looks at my tub and goes ohhh you need a plumber to remove the tub. Daniel is a tub fixer not a plumber. Daniel gave suggestions on what the problem could be but my plumber said \" when the water gets to the jets that's when it starts leaking. Get this guy to just fix that \" I told Daniel this and he insisted on testing it himself. Which is more then fair but I told him I don't want a 500 dollar bill to be right in the same place. It's a leak you need to get under the tub to fix and we can't move forward without the tub beijg lifted..\n\nSo I asked him how much I owe him now for this wonderful advise and it's 100 dollars for him to show and 100 dollars in consultation fees + tax = 240.\n\nSo for him to do nothing I'm out 240 dollars. I called my plumber who recommended me this guy and told him the story and he was embarrassed.\n\nI emailed him asking him if I could remove 100 dollars cause he did nothing. I'd pay him 100 just to show up. He argued that's what it costs I had to pay. I emailed him back saying my plumber will never use him again. What he's doing is fraud and my tub is an easy 1000+ dollar job to do. Why he was so insistent on me paying 240 for his showing up is beyond me when if he tried to actually do his job he could have made way more.\n\nHe has emailed me 3 times since justifying what he did and saying should I need him again no charge and I keep telling him I will never use his services again",
        "time": 1654864580,
        "translated": false
      },
